{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghJBvdcDZeXb6X2B9yMh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\nFeature: Every project page stops drawing the progress bar under its done percent,\non desktop rows and on phone cards, and keeps the percent, which gets louder as it\nrises. The developer says the bar \"takes up room\" without \"earning it\", so the page\ngets that room back and the number alone carries the fact.\n\nAs a team lead, I want the done percent to get louder as it climbs past 60%,\nso that I can spot a project that is nearly finished without reading a bar beside it.\n\nProblem: Every project row and card draws a bar under DONE beside the percent. Its\ntone turns at 50%, the same point where the percent turns strong. So the bar repeats\nthe number, takes width on desktop and height on a phone, and does not separate a\n64% from a 92%.\n\nWill not do:\n- the milestone page's DONE, which counts milestones, a different fact with no bar;\n- the burndown chart, which the developer keeps;\n- the member pages. Their activity cards draw histograms, not this bar.\n\nSettled:\n- \"the bar under the done percent takes up room and is not earning it\" (request)\n- \"the number could get louder as it gets higher, starting around 60\" (request)\n- Asked how it gets louder, the developer chose \"A continuous ramp\": 42% faint, 64%\n  slightly warmer, 78% warmer, 92% full accent (request)\n- \"colours come from the theme tokens only\" (AGENTS.md:40)\n```\n\nThree questions about what counts as done:\n\n1. **Where does the percent reach full colour?** The request says the ramp runs from 60% to full accent at 100%. Your example puts 92% at full accent. On a 60→100 ramp, 92% is only 80% of the way. Should it reach full at 100%, or at about 90% and hold there?\n\n2. **What happens to 50–59%?** Today anything at 50% or above reads in the strong foreground colour, and under 50% reads faint. If the ramp starts at 60 and 42% is faint, 50–59% drops from strong to faint. Is that what you want, with everything under 60% one flat faint?\n\n3. **Does the overdue column ramp the same?** On a project with a deadline, the OVERDUE column shows the share of tasks past due. Should a 78% OVERDUE get the same warmth as a 78% DONE? Projects without a deadline show only DONE.\n\nI'll stop here until you correct or answer these."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1617,"cache_read_input_tokens":79290,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1617},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d927ec62-fc1a-4016-9073-c3b01d3098bc","uuid":"bc536b9a-f957-4137-b53e-3abf69f9f020","timestamp":"2026-11-04T04:59:14.239Z","request_id":"req_011CghJBvQDBQDhSbKCBJGdT"}
